DECISIONS.md:5:- **2026-07-18 — DOPAMINE DIRECTION RATIFIED (Allen, playtest #13 conversation; memo `docs/6-memo/2026-07-18-dopamine-direction.md`).** The sweat-repetitiveness moment design/04's v0 note asked to record has arrived (run: playtest #13, "could feel boring... CloverPit pays every spin"). Rulings on the memo's five levers: (1) **micro-markets ratified as the cadence fix** — corners/next-goal/player props resolving mid-leg, its own post-slice TRIP HIGH plan with engine + sim campaign ("once we have micro-markets it should be more fun"); (2) **M-T4/M-T5 confirmed** as the dopamine milestones (taunting counter, momentum tape, settle payoffs, crowd audio); (3) **partial cash-out REJECTED as a baseline verb** — "irl we can't do that"; the diegetic-realism bar applies to book mechanics, not just presentation. May return RELIC-GATED (a relic that sells you a non-real-book power is fair game — same doctrine as Ask for the Manager's human-agency exemption); parked, revisit with the Band-2 agency work; (4) **Band-3 number-go-up spectacle ratified** (renderer-only); (5) **RedZone multi-sweat cut ratified** (lategame density, presentation-only). Sequencing stands: M-T4 → M-T5 → micro-markets plan; spectacle and RedZone ride along where they fit.
DECISIONS.md:7:- **2026-07-18 — MATCH THEATER RULING: the sweat gets a 2D stage; the "no field, no players" clause of 2026-07-07 is SUPERSEDED (Allen, plan F_0.2.0).** After nine playtests Allen's verdict: text validated pacing but is not enough for the near-final signature moment. The reframe that makes this safe: the theater is **a renderer of the drama stream, not a sports simulation** — design/04's tier-3 "abstract momentum viz" matured into a stage with actors (the ball's field position IS territory), while the tier-4 content-pipeline trap stays cut via the theater laws: every staged moment keyed by a `DramaEvent`; idle filler never signifies (restates revealed state, never implies new information); presentation-local RNG only; causal score synthesis (goals commit on scene playback; suspended finals resolve from the final ticket-local grade; every ledger increment maps 1:1 to a staged goal; live-lead clamp ±1 — the theater tells one-goal-game stories); stakes chrome stays dominant; palette law extended (no red team dots, no money-green pitch, VAR-disallow never a red card). Grill rulings: soccer stage; fewer-bigger beats; momentum tape in slice; WebGL/itch deferred to a follow-up plan; beats 3–8s tension-paced, 60–90s per full-density 3-leg sweat, final-leg ×2 kept. Process of record: TRIP HIGH — Sol plan review ran 5 rounds to APPROVED (11 findings, all accepted; PLAN-REVIEW-LOG.md). **M-T1 engine change shipped same day:** budgets 5–10 → 3–5/leg with a progressive-density ramp (2–4 at round 1 → full band at round 3, `EventBoundsForRound`, AwayFromZero + both-branch clamps), `BuildTicketPaths` takes the 1-based round. Drama-stream goldens re-pinned INTENTIONALLY (GOLDEN-W2: 47 → 18 events; near-miss pins re-scanned to NM2-10/SC-99); the settlement pin (bank 428.631019) deliberately untouched and green — the outcome-invariance proof. Engine tests 146/146. Sim gate campaign on TUNE- seeds pending; HOLDOUT3- validation deferred until after Allen's console texture