DECISIONS.md:9:- **2026-07-15 — CHARM EXPANSION SHIPPED: 17 new items, the dealt-hand shop, Ref's Whistle — ALL GATES PASS on held-out seeds (sim-report-4-holdout2.md, 7.55M runs).** The stacking-strategies pillar at prototype scale: catalog 15 passives + 7 consumables = 22 items (CloverPit-inspired by mandate; Same Game Special CUT by Allen pre-build). Process of record: /grill-me-codex — Act 1 grill locked Whistle semantics (grading re-roll in the pending window, ticket-local, full odds on an overturn), the sim bar, the one-modifier law, dealt-hand rules; Act 2 Codex adversarial review ran 5 rounds to APPROVED (46 findings; Codex won the G4-contract and terminal-credit arguments, conceded Photo-prices-cash-outs; the whole exchange in PLAN-REVIEW-LOG.md). Engine: typed effect pipeline, named factor maps in the one product slot, integer deci-comps, DeriveRng, terminal-realization ledger, House Key payment getters. Sim: paired-seed CI flags (Bonferroni), exposure thresholds, G6 worst-case granted martyr, archetype telemetry bots. TWO RE-RATIFICATIONS DURING THE CAMPAIGN (Allen): G3 median re-banded ≥6 → ≥5 (the dealt hand's build variance IS the roguelite shape — median-6 was jointly unreachable with the naive/noshop bands); G4 gates on PASSIVE-ONLY counterfactual EV (cheap +EV promos are the catalog's fantasy — full-contract EV measured time-to-first-promo; logged amendment, Codex-sanctioned branch). Tuned numbers: Multiplier ×1.6, Chalk 2pp, Jar 10pp, System 12pp, comps 0.12/$, R5 payment 155, hand 4P+3C, Bobblehead 2×. Holdout protocol honored the hard way: HOLDOUT burned when the Manager's DEAD flag was declared playtest-gated (Timeout precedent — bot-unmonetizable agency), HOLDOUT2 revalidated clean from commit dfb588d. Holdout facts: skilled 7.0% / median 5 (stable across three seed families), martyr-worst 5.9% under the +2pp guard, totem organic 37.5%, G5 excess +0.1pp (passes the ratified >0; MISSES the rev-3 protocol margin of +0.5 — documented, not hidden: the Multiplier+Scar synergy is real but hair-thin). Campaign findings of record: pre-engine buy discipline beats any item; reserving toward future payments LOWERS survival (the income race punishes timidity); granted-free Free Bet/Parachute audit NEGATIVE on win rate (insurance crowds out compounding) — playtest watch items, not nerf targets. Engine tests 144/144; Unity 32/32 + 8/8; console smoke green. Gate: playtest #9.
DECISIONS.md:10:- **2026-07-13 — PLAYTEST #8: TIMEOUT CUT; TOTEM REWORKED TO FULL DEFERRAL — gates re-held (sim-report-3.md, 50k/batch).** Allen's two findings, both shipped same day. (1) Timeout removed end to end (Allen: "useless"; the sim's audit read ≈0 all along — playtest-gated, playtest voted no). The catalog is 3 passives + 2 consumables; the engine's live-intervention seam (`ApplyLiveEffect`/`OfferHoldEffect`) survives under its own test as future-actives plumbing. (2) The Totem no longer takes the bank: Allen fired it and landed at $0 — a zombie round (below the $10 min stake, mercy in name only). New behavior: the whole payment DEFERS — bank untouched, payment × (1 + juice 0.5) added to the next payment, still never the final round. Campaign discovery: the resulting G3 breach (skilled 9.2% > 8%) traced NOT to the totem (+0.3pp audit) but to the Timeout cut itself — a 2-item catalog under 2 shop offer slots guaranteed a Mulligan Slip (+20pp audit item) every visit. Fix at the offer draw, where the cause was: consumable offers 2 → 1 per shop, consumable slots 2 → 3, mulligan 2 → 1.5 comps; payment curve and comps rate untouched. Result: skilled 6.2% (band 5–8%), organic totem fire 50.3%, zero item flags — and the totem-flag check now reads the ORGANIC fire rate, encoding the artifact rationale ratified narratively in sim-report-2.
DECISIONS.md:12:- **2026-07-12 — M5 SHIPPED: the phone is the bookie (first Codex-built milestone).** Design locked via /grill-me-codex (grill with Allen → 5 adversarial Codex review rounds → APPROVED; full argument in PLAN-REVIEW-LOG.md), then Codex implemented PLAN.md rev 4 under /codex-build with Claude verifying (production code needed zero fixes; 42/42 tests). Decisions of record: phone = the bookie's VOICE (text thread, not an info hub — but float texts DO name the owed amount, pinned to DebtAfter); a person, warm→cold deadpan arc (VIP-host satire parked); DeskFocus reused top-down (pick-up-into-hand deferred to the juice pass); nine trigger kinds with subtype-complete deterministic keys; visual-only buzz until the sound pass. CORRECTION shipped: debt is a one-round loan (Settle clears or collects — Run.cs), so escalation rides on repeat-float coldness + the indebted-round beat + the final-round warning, not per-round reminders. DeskFocus hardened en route: per-instance prompts, claim-before-glide camera ownership, OnDisable unwind. Known gap logged for backlog: SitSpot remains outside the focus-ownership domain (pre-existing M4 seam, low risk).
DECISIONS.md:13:- **2026-07-11 — M4 design locked by grill session (Allen confirmed): the real betting loop, in-room.** Scope: a full run playable start-to-finish in the room, no console; the phone stays a stub until M5; the demo channel is deleted (`DemoTicketPolicy` survives as the test/auto-play fixture). **Laptop** = E-zoom + free cursor, no sit (high-frequency surface wants low ceremony; the couch keeps the only sit ritual) with phase-driven pages that railroad like a real betting app: BETSLIP (two-panel sportsbook layout, one working slip, fraction-chip stakes 10%/25%/50%/MAX + $10 nudges — uncapped all-in stays one deliberate click; LOCK IT IN with a one-step zero-ticket confirm), GO WATCH while locked, SHOP, RUN OVER with NEW RUN (**prototype flow only — Allen: a proper menu will own run restart later**); persistent header row: round/bank/target/debt-in-red + relic strip + piggy. **TV** walks the round's sweats serially: ~2s auto-advance ticket cards between sweats (design/04's no-prompts law holds — the sweat stays hands-off watchable), a settle card after the last (TARGET MET green / THE BOOKIE FLOATS YOU red), then SHOP OPEN while the laptop lid breathes for attention; the run verdict lands on the TV with the room light dropping cold on a loss, gold on the win (the cheap lighting fake of design/08's room states). Inherited: zero-ticket locks settle on the spot; E cash-out applies only to the currently sweating ticket. Why: proves the full loop on the diegetic surfaces with the walk between couch and desk as the loop's rhythm — the room is the interface.
DECISIONS.md:14:- **2026-07-11 — M3 design decisions (the TV plays the sweat, live from the real engine).** (1) A demo channel feeds the screen until M4: `DemoRunDriver` runs real `Run`/`SweatSession` state end to end (place → lock → sweat → settle → shop-skip → next, new run on win/loss) with a deterministic `DemoTicketPolicy` (2–3 shortest-priced legs, 25% of bank) that consumes no engine RNG. (2) The TV stops being an interactable — it IS the sweat surface: a code-built world-space UGUI canvas on the screen inset, no assets. (3) The sweat steps only while seated — sitting starts/resumes, standing pauses mid-event with the offer frozen (design/04 "Diegetic viewing"). (4) Presentation never consumes engine RNG (only MoveNext/CashOut; outcomes stay baked at lock). (5) design/08 palette law enforced on the first real surface: green = money-good only, red = money-bad only, gold = cash-out; the TvLight makes the room the reaction shot. (6) While a cash-out offer is live, E accepts it and the couch's stand-up is suppressed (standing = hold-move). Why: proves the emotional core on the diegetic surface with the real engine before any betting UI exists, and keeps determinism intact for the WebGL golden-seed check.
DECISIONS.md:16:- **2026-07-10 — Art direction DECIDED (Allen): betting-app diegesis framed by a compact room (design/08).** All UI diegetic (sweat on the TV, betslip at the desk, bookie as phone notifications); casino neon on black (green=money-good, red=money-bad, gold=cash-out, colors reserved); room = health bar with ~4 states (Tokyo compact, no kitchen: bunk bed over couch, TV opposite, window beside, mini fridge + desk) — slice ships state 1 + a lighting/decal fake of the debt states. Game name: SBR codename until Phase 3.
DECISIONS.md:18:- **2026-07-09 — Recalibration landed: S3 PASS (naive median death 3), S4 PASS (skilled median death 7, win 11.5%).** Final §8: targets [400,460,520,650,800,1000,1500,2800], juice 0.5, prices 150–250, bank/overround/margin unchanged. Known residuals for Week 6: random's median matches naive's (debt punishes wild sizing hardest — acceptable, G3 half-met); skilled's organic EV-arc never crosses zero (survival-optimal bot buys surplus-only; whether looser human buying recovers the arc is a playtest question); relic audit at the new config ranks insurance dominant (+4.3pp win) and mulligan dead (±0) — both feed the item rework.
DECISIONS.md:19:- **2026-07-09 — Debt-as-HP failure model APPROVED (Allen).** Miss a target with no debt → the bookie floats you: bank topped up to the target (working capital), debt = shortfall × (1 + juice rate, default 0.5, sim-tuned). Clearing target + debt at a later settle repays it in cash. Miss while already in debt = run over. No borrowing on the final round. Rationale: converts geometric instant-death into accumulating pressure so runs reach the relic-compounding band; thematically native (the bookie).
DECISIONS.md:22:- **2026-07-09 — Week 5 sim findings accepted as the tuning agenda; target retune deferred into Week 6 alongside the item rework.** S3/S4 both FAIL on current §8 targets (all strategies median death 1). A flat-early curve experiment ([520…2600]) improved skilled to median death 2 — direction confirmed, magnitude insufficient → the failure model itself is on the table (debt-as-HP proposal) plus book-noise pricing for the information axis; both parked in OPEN-QUESTIONS for Allen. Relic audit re-runs after retune.
DECISIONS.md:23:- **2026-07-08 — Max stake cap LIFTED (Allen, playtest #1); High Roller redesigned to an all-in payout bonus.** Reverses the same-day 50%-of-bank cap: stakes now uncapped to the whole bank (MaxStakeFraction default 1.0, kept as a /sim dial). Since the cap removal made High Roller's cap-doubling a no-op (again), it becomes: staking ≥ half your bank boosts that ticket's payout +15% (Ticket.PayoutMultiplier; scales win payout and cash-out fair value, never stake-based partials).
DECISIONS.md:24:- **2026-07-08 — Item system direction (Allen, playtest #1): split relics into one-time-use consumables vs permanent passive skills,** separate slot pools, sell-back. Rationale: 5/5 permanents felt too easy; consumables restore scarcity decisions. Designed in design/03; implementation timing parked in OPEN-QUESTIONS (lean: post-Week-5 sim, rebalance measured, verdict on the reworked system).
DECISIONS.md:26:- **2026-07-08 — Sharp Eye redesigned: "+EV flag" → exact true-prob reveal for one chosen line per round.** Implementation proved the spec'd predicate `trueProb × offeredOdds > 1` is mathematically always false against our sharp vig-priced book (F3: no mispricing exists to find), making the relic dead content and undermining S5. Same id/axis/price/charge; now the active, exact counterpart to Tout Sheet's passive fuzzy intervals. Found by the Week 3 implementation agent.
DECISIONS.md:27:- **2026-07-08 — Accepted v0 imprecision: cash-out fair value ignores Lucky Charm's +3pp on the final leg.** Pricing the baked roll correctly would leak the future through the offer; the unconditional underprice is conservative (house-favorable). Revisit if a lucky-charm cash-out build emerges in sim.
DECISIONS.md:28:- **2026-07-08 — Week 3 scope decisions (pre-implementation).** (a) Base max stake = 50% of current bank per ticket; High Roller doubles to 100% (PRD §8 amended — original spec made it a no-op). (b) Lucky Charm = per-ticket second-chance reroll on a lost final leg at `0.03/(1−p)` — exactly +3pp, preserves the fixed universe and shared-outcome invariant; only your slip's grading bends. (c) Mulligan auto-applies (pure buff, no real decision in v0), multi-leg tickets only; player-choice variant deferred to console UX. (d) Piggy Bank accrues only positive vig (Boosted Odds/Promo Code can drive vig ≤ 0). (e) Relic content = C# catalog (op + params + price), not JSON: System.Text.Json isn't in netstandard2.1 and adds Unity/IL2CPP friction; same data shape, zero dependencies; externalize when content scales. (f) New dedicated `Relics` RNG stream; effect resolution strictly in acquisition order.
DECISIONS.md:29:- **2026-07-07 — Relic timing classes (pre-game / live / passive) + "store the base, compute the effective."** Locked odds are the contract and never mutate; live effects layer modifiers through the effect pipeline. Live `p` manipulation runs through the drama generator's intervention seam (conditional re-sample + re-author). Week 2 builds the sweat as a steppable cursor (needed for cash-out regardless); the seam ships unused in v0.
DECISIONS.md:31:- **2026-07-07 — Cash-out fair-value formula corrected** in design/02: remaining legs contribute `p_j × o_j`, not `p_j` alone. Caught during engine implementation; both sanity anchors (none-resolved, all-resolved) are now unit tests.
DECISIONS.md:37:- **2026-07-07 — Signature mechanic: the sweat.** Leg-by-leg parlay resolution with live cash-out offer. Design Pillar 1; all juice budget flows here first.
DECISIONS.md:38:- **2026-07-07 — Sports are not simulated; drama is.** Outcome sampled first from true p, then a pacing-controlled narrative generator writes events arriving at it. Live p / cash-out math stays honest. Makes multi-sport support a reskin.
DECISIONS.md:39:- **2026-07-07 — Every mechanic maps to the four-number model** (true p, offered odds, stake, payout) and one of five axes (information / odds / capital / resolution / economy).
DECISIONS.md:43:- **2026-07-07 — Economy doctrine: the EV arc with three bands** (Allen's direction, formalized in design/02). Band 1 scarcity balanced tight; Band 3 "sanctioned brokenness" deliberately uncapped — gate *when* it's reachable, never *how high*. Synergy audits classify loops (delicious vs degenerate), they don't kill them. Anti-grind: layered progression; across-run unlocks lean breadth-not-power (prestige final call still OPEN).
DECISIONS.md:44:- **2026-07-07 — Pillar 3 generalized: "four numbers" → "mathematically legible payoff functions."** Allen's counterexamples (per-leg payout relic retaining full parlay payout; 2× vig-rebate piggy bank) are strong designs that don't fit scalar modification of p/o/s/payout. New law: relics may rewrite a bet's payoff function or operate on tracked run-level accounting quantities, provided the effect is expressible at existing engine hooks and EV-auditable by /sim. Derived rule added to 02: cash-out prices the full remaining payoff function, including future relic cash flows.
design/04-the-sweat.md:10:2. A **drama generator** then writes a plausible event sequence (score changes, momentum swings, injuries, "they're mounting a comeback") that *arrives at* the predetermined outcome.
design/04-the-sweat.md:13:Integrity rule: the drama never changes the sampled outcome (unless an Axis-4 relic explicitly and visibly does). Live `p` shown to the player is the honest conditional probability given events so far — the cash-out math stays truthful even though the storyline is authored. Players will reverse-engineer the system; it must be defensible.
design/04-the-sweat.md:19:Allen's worry: "build a parlay, wait, hit or not" is boring without footage. The answer is not simulating footage — it's fidelity to the real fantasy: **a bettor doesn't watch the game, he watches the app.** The live win-probability graph, the scorebug, the cash-out number — betting apps and ESPN have already trained the audience to sweat from exactly this interface. For our satire it's also the joke: the degenerate stares at the betslip, not the game.
