design/04-the-sweat.md:43:**Multi-ticket presentation — "the wall":** the round's games display as a sportsbook-lobby wall of mini scorebugs; a **director system** cuts focus to the highest-tension moment (the RedZone pattern), driven by the drama generator's tension tags. This resolves the serial-vs-parallel question as a hybrid: parallel wall, directed serial focus. Engine requirement: drama generator emits tension scores; director is a presentation-layer policy over them.
design/04-the-sweat.md:47:Anti-boredom invariant: the player is never purely waiting — the cash-out offer is a live decision held open through the whole sweat, and every event moves it.
design/04-the-sweat.md:49:## Mid-sweat agency ladder (PROPOSED 2026-07-07 — answers "is cash-out alone enough?")
design/04-the-sweat.md:55:| 1 — mark | watches, prays | full cash-out only. The powerlessness IS the tension (thematically honest) |
design/04-the-sweat.md:56:| 2 — operator | intervenes | relic **active charges**: Timeout (pause drama, lock offer for 3 events), Ref's Whistle (veto + reroll one event), momentum boost; **partial cash-out** (real sportsbook feature — take 50%, let half ride); director remote in multi-ticket rounds |
design/04-the-sweat.md:59:Hard rule: **no QTEs.** Mid-sweat actions are options, never prompts; the sweat stays fully watchable hands-off. Required input converts tension into task.
design/04-the-sweat.md:63:Engine cost: near zero — active charges are player-initiated effects on the existing `OnMatchEvent` / `OnCashOutOffered` hooks.
design/04-the-sweat.md:65:v0 note: prototype ships cash-out-only *on purpose* (isolates the anticipation+one-decision hypothesis). Evaluation should record **when** sweat repetitiveness first appears (which run #) as design input for this ladder.
